{"t":9389,"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChALYyo2TJVKLiRFHyxvG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bash command printed `NONCE=36182905`.\n\nThe electric telegraph grew out of experiments in the 1830s, when several inventors realized that electrical current could carry messages over wire. In Britain, William Fothergill Cooke and Charles Wheatstone built a needle telegraph that used deflecting magnetized needles to point at letters, and it was first used commercially on the London and Birmingham railway in 1839. In the United States, Samuel Morse worked with Alfred Vail on a different approach: a single wire carrying short and long pulses that were coded as dots and dashes. Morse's system, which became known as Morse code, was demonstrated in 1838, and in 1844 he sent the first public long-distance message, \"What hath God wrought,\" from Washington to Baltimore.\n\nThe telegraph spread quickly because it separated communication from transportation. Before it, a message could travel no faster than a horse, a ship or a train. Within a few decades, telegraph lines followed railway tracks across continents, and in 1866 a cable finally linked Britain and North America reliably, after earlier attempts had failed. Newspapers relied on telegraphic dispatches, financial markets used ticker machines to share prices, and governments used the wires for military and diplomatic traffic. The American Civil War and the colonial administration of distant territories both depended heavily on it.\n\nThe telegraph also changed how people thought about distance and time. Clocks in cities began to be synchronized through wires, and standard time zones were eventually adopted partly to coordinate railways and telegraph reports. Its successors, the telephone and then radio, built on the same principle of turning information into electrical signals, and the basic idea of encoding a message as a sequence of simple signals still underlies digital communication today."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3864,"cache_read_input_tokens":24182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3864},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad0db25e-4992-4db0-8d55-7b8bda54f719","uuid":"23e32431-c2ac-43b0-bd1b-eac9b18dc4b6","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:45:35.085Z","request_id":"req_011ChALYyVAxU1YJSaNEBQjA"}
